  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "When the heat of a reaction at constant pressure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cal</mi></math>&nbsp;and entropy change for the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cal</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mo>deg</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>,&nbsp;it is predicted that the reaction at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>25</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "E1FZO",
      "text": "revesible",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "pN4ii",
      "text": "spontaneous",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oTQld",
      "text": "non-spontaneous",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hnbZj",
      "text": "irreversible",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Heat at constant pressure means enthalpy. i.e.,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;G</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>T&#916;S</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>cal</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>caldeg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;G</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>T&#916;S</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>298</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4705</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cal</mi></math></p><p>As the value of&nbsp;&Delta;G&nbsp;is&nbsp;&minus;4705.2&nbsp;cal, which is a negative value, so this reaction will be spontaneous.&nbsp;</p><p>Hence, the process is spontaneous.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
